{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph stored as adjacency lists, the undirected counterpart of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices. Self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same edge as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. While the vertices are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order, each is its own slot and there is no dictionary. Edges are kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an array, so an edge’s position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each slot has a row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop is in its vertex’s row twice. The rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices it has. The bulk initializers ("},{"code":"init(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"init(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"init(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"init(adjacency:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the builder and the dictionary literal) lay every row out once at its exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, in slot order; a row that later outgrows its block moves to the end. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position answers "},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(1) expected."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1). The last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, edge order and edge positions are therefore unspecified and may change after a removal."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Maps attached to the graph ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addEdgeMap(default:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph"},{"type":"text","text":") move their values with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/undirectedadjacencylist"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule010UndirectedaB0V","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}],"modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift#L26"},"symbolKind":"stru